  1 | select * from t {alias};
    | select * from t $a_____;
  2 | select * from t {}{}, t {0}_x;
    | select * from t $bc_, t $b_x_;

placeholders:
     16..23 `{alias}` -> `$a_____` value
     41..45 `{}{}` -> `$bc_` value
     49..54 `{0}_x` -> `$b_x_` value

diagnostics:
  16..23 `{alias}`: A template placeholder directly after `t` can't be read: write `AS` before an alias; a placeholder can stand for a name or a value, not a SQL clause.
  41..45 `{}{}`: A template placeholder directly after `t` can't be read: write `AS` before an alias; a placeholder can stand for a name or a value, not a SQL clause.
  49..54 `{0}_x`: A template placeholder directly after `t` can't be read: write `AS` before an alias; a placeholder can stand for a name or a value, not a SQL clause.
